---
import '../design/design-aids.css';
import SketchSheet from '../design/SketchSheet.astro';
import SketchArrow from '../design/SketchArrow.astro';
---
<figure id="retry-commit-reply" class="design-aid design-figure paper-surface" aria-labelledby="retry-commit-title">
  <span class="plate-number">Illustration · A missing answer</span>
  <h3 id="retry-commit-title">The same silence can follow two endings</h3>
  <p>The application sends COMMIT for checkout K14. Its connection then fails before an answer arrives. These are alternative histories, not two simultaneous purchases.</p>
  <div class="reply-alternatives">
    <div><SketchSheet tone="teal"><h4>History 1 · committed</h4><p>Order O14 and stock reduction <strong>kept</strong>.</p><p>The database’s reply is lost.</p></SketchSheet><div class="reply-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><span>No reply reaches the application</span></div></div>
    <div><SketchSheet tone="amber"><h4>History 2 · not committed</h4><p>COMMIT never takes effect. The abandoned transaction’s changes are <strong>discarded</strong>.</p><p>No success reply exists.</p></SketchSheet><div class="reply-arrow"><SketchArrow direction="down" /><span>No reply reaches the application</span></div></div>
  </div>
  <SketchSheet tone="blue"><h4>What the application knows</h4><p>“I have no commit result for K14.”</p><p>Use K14 to find or safely resume the same checkout. A new key would describe another operation.</p></SketchSheet>
  <figcaption>A broken connection alone does not identify which history happened. A stable key and database uniqueness can coordinate a repeated database checkout; recovery still has to consult authoritative state. Payment providers and other services have separate outcomes and require their own reconciliation.</figcaption>
</figure>
<style>
  .reply-alternatives { display:grid; grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr; gap:1rem; margin-top:1.2rem; }
  .reply-arrow { display:flex; align-items:center; gap:.5rem; margin:.7rem 0; font-size:.75rem; color:var(--color-text-secondary); }
  @media(max-width:520px) { .reply-alternatives { grid-template-columns:1fr; } }
</style>
